<subsection> 
 <title>Preliminary formulas</title>
<p>
<ul>
<li><m>x_i </m> is the value of the <m>i</m>th observation for the variable of interest.</li>
<li><m>n</m> is the sample size.</li>
<li><m>\overline{x} = \frac{\text{sum of observations in the sample}}{n} = \frac{\sum x_i  }{n} = \frac{x_1 + \ldots + x_n }{n} </m> is the sample mean, which is a measure of center for a sample. The sample mean is sometimes called the average.</li>
<li><m>\displaystyle s = \sqrt{ \frac{\sum (x_i - \overline{x})^2 }{n-1}  } = \sqrt{ \frac{ (x_1 - \overline{x})^2 + \ldots + (x_n - \overline{x})^2  }{n-1}  } </m> is the sample standard deviation, which is a measure of the typical deviation of the data values from the mean for a sample.</li>
</ul>
</p>
</subsection>

